<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  HolyFlame_RitualistWiring.xml      UtinniPatches — SUMP_UTINNI_LAYER_1 §2

  Makes RUT_HolyFlame_Revered (PreceptDefs/RUT_HolyFlamePrecepts.xml)
  selectable at all. RimWorld/MemeDef.cs (decompiled, read in full):
  `requireOne` is a List<List<PreceptDef>> — an ideoligion only ever gets
  offered a precept that appears inside SOME meme's requireOne group, there
  is no "show every precept under this issue" fallback. Shipping the precept
  without this patch would be silently unreachable content.

  `Ritualist` (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/data/ideology_palette.md line 81:
  impact 2, source Anomaly — MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly", NOT core
  Ideology) is the closest-fitting existing meme: an ideoligion that already
  cares about ritual observance is the natural home for one more ritual
  option. This appends a NEW group (one more <li> in the outer list) holding
  only this one precept — it does not touch or reorder Ritualist's existing
  groups.

  This makes the precept selectable by ANY ideoligion (player-authored or
  NPC-generated) that takes the Ritualist meme — it is NOT retroactively
  added to the campaign's own saved ideoligion ("The Salvation"). See
  RUT_HolyFlamePrecepts.xml's own header for why that is a separate, live,
  manual action and not this patch's scope.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
    <xpath>Defs/MemeDef[defName="Ritualist"]/requireOne</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/MemeDef[defName="Ritualist"]/requireOne</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>
          <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">RUT_HolyFlame_Revered</li>
        </li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
